,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-04T03:49:37Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T12:13:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.7.2\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 - Godot v4.7.2.stable - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070\n\n### Issue description\n\nTitle explains it, but SpriteFrames's set_animation_speed/updating animation speed in the inspector does not call emit_changed. I'm trying to make a particle system that takes data from a SpriteFrames + extra options and I need the particle data to be updated when SpriteFrames's animation speed is changed (esp. in the inspector) and as it stands that's not possible without a previous state workaround in _process.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a function that prints a statement.\nConnect the function to a spriteframes.changed\nUpdate the animation speed in the inspector to find no function call\n\n<img width=\"196\" height=\"103\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/939f1218-d88d-49ba-a60f-1ba9323a422d\" />\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp_2026-10-03_23-48-46.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33016697/mrp_2026-10-03_23-48-46.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124143/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rock